@startuml
title Sequence - release publication and distribution (success + failure)

actor Maintainer
participant "main (GitHub)" as main
participant "Release Process\n(GitHub Actions)" as release
participant "npm registry" as npm
participant "dist branch\n(orphan, force-pushed)" as dist
actor User
participant "AI assistant\n(Claude Code / Copilot CLI)" as assistant

Maintainer -> main: merge PR (Conventional Commit)
main -> release: push triggers the workflow

release -> release: release-please creates tag/Release vX.Y.Z
release -> npm: npm publish\n(prepublishOnly: build+lint+test+golden)

alt Publish succeeds
    npm --> release: OK
    release -> release: build dist/ from the published tag
    release -> dist: force-push the snapshot (source + dist/)
    dist --> release: OK

    ...later, on any install...
    User -> assistant: marketplace install command
    assistant -> main: reads .claude-plugin/marketplace.json
    main --> assistant: source.ref = dist
    assistant -> dist: fetches the plugin content from that ref
    dist --> assistant: files ready (dist/ present, no local build)
    assistant --> User: plugin installed and working on first use
else Publish fails (build, lint, test or golden test break)
    npm --> release: error
    release -> release: aborts - dist branch is NOT touched
    note right of dist
        The last intact version
        stays available; no
        partial version is ever
        exposed (RN-02, RN-04)
    end note
end
@enduml
